  "question": {
    "text": "Two coils have a mutual inductance <math><mn>0.005</mn><mi>&nbsp;</mi><mn>H</mn><mo>.</mo></math> The current changes in the first coil according to equation <math><mi>I</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mi>I</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">sin</mi></mrow><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>ω</mi><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfenced></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></math> where <math><msub><mrow><mi>I</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>10&nbsp;</mn><mn>A</mn></math> and <math><mi>ω</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>100</mn><mi>π</mi><mi>&nbsp;</mi><mi>rad</mi><mi>&nbsp;</mi><msup><mrow><mn>s</mn></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>.</mo></math> The maximum value of emf in the second coil is"
